    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что ты здесь делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you doing here?' A compact expression built around 'what' and 'are you doing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Что не на работе?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why aren't you at work?' Here 'what' sets up the idea, while 'work' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Опять допрос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Another interrogation.' Here 'again' sets up the idea, while 'interrogation' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы сговорились что ли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you plan this or something?' Kostya puts 'you' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'conspired'. Max answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Я сегодня во вторую смену.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am on the second shift today.' The key word here means 'I', which Max combines with 'today'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично. Я с тобой поеду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Great. I will go with you.' Kostya starts with 'perfect' and pairs it with 'I' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Может ты забыл,",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Maybe you forgot,' Max starts with 'can' and pairs it with 'you' to make the point clear. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, я помню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yeah, I remember.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'remember' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Меня уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I got fired.' The first content word means 'me', and 'to fire' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "А что ты не у Вики остался?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why didn't you stay at Vika's?' Max starts with 'what' and pairs it with 'you' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "max",
      "t": "Она меня не пустила.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She wouldn't let me in.' You'll hear 'it' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to let go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Она все усложнять начала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She started making everything complicated.' The first content word means 'it', and 'beginning' rounds out the thought.",
